[
    {
        "content": "<p>I would like to use <code>FunLike</code> for a bundled function of two variables (curry'd), but I run into an issue when trying to get this to work with <code>fun_prop</code>. The error thrown is in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Mathlib.Meta.FunProp.getTheoremFromConst#doc\">docs#Mathlib.Meta.FunProp.getTheoremFromConst</a> and <code>fun_prop</code> seems to not like over-applied arguments. I would be interested in the reason for that and whether it is possible to make the example below work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Constructions</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SumProd</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cont'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uncurry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instFunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FunLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe_injective'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">congr</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">fun_prop</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuous</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cont'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hg₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prodMk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hg₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- fails with: fun_prop theorem about morphism coercion has to be in fully applied form</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 582709117,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1774936152
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it is overly defensive here. It dose some basic sanity check to help write theorems in the correct form but in this case the check is wrong. It should let the theorem be registered. This case just did not come up yet.</p>",
        "id": 582712801,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1774938249
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you think removing the over-applied check is fine? Or does it have to be replaced with something way more sophisticated?</p>",
        "id": 582713475,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1774938577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If i understand correctly it might be a user facing sanity check when tagging, looking at the actual application source in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Mathlib.Meta.FunProp.applyMorRules#doc\">docs#Mathlib.Meta.FunProp.applyMorRules</a> it seems to handle <code>.overapplied</code> correctly:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">overApplied</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fData</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">peeloffArgDecomposition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">applyCompRule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">funPropDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">funProp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>in the source for the sanity check in <code>Mathlib.Tactic.FunProp.Theorems</code> it does have a </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- todo: maybe do a little bit more careful detection of morphism and transition theorems</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>You could try not throwing an error and  something like <code>return .mor thm </code> instead , it might work or might break spectacularly. As far as I see though there is a small chance it could work.</p>",
        "id": 582722001,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1774942191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, exactly I think we can just turn that check off and likely everything will work fine.</p>",
        "id": 582731349,
        "sender_full_name": "Tomas Skrivan",
        "timestamp": 1774943858
    },
